 step or help you run the checks on actual files.\\n\\nWhat I can check beyond the text\\n- Text content (robust checks): per-page text, ordering, and subtle differences like extra spaces, hyphenation, or line breaks.\\n- Non-text elements: embedded images, hyperlinks, and annotations.\\n- Metadata and structure: document info (title, author, subject, dates), XMP metadata, fonts embedded, and object structure.\\n- Fonts and rendering: which fonts are embedded, font subset, and whether the same glyphs render identically.\\n- Visual differences: pixel-level differences when rendered to images.\\n\\nHow to perform a thorough comparison (step-by-step)\\n\\n1) Extract and compare text (per-page)\\n- Use Poppler:\\n  - pdftotext -layout file1.pdf file1.txt\\n  - pdftotext -layout file2.pdf file2.txt\\n- Compare:\\n  - diff -u file1.txt file2.txt\\n- If you suspect non-visible characters, normalize first:\\n  - Normalize Unicode and normalize whitespace, then diff.\\n\\n2) Compare metadata and structure\\n- Metadata and basic info:\\n  - pdfinfo file1.pdf\\n  - pdfinfo file2.pdf\\n- XMP metadata (if present):\\n  - exiftool -X -a -u -b file1.pdf\\n  - exiftool -X -a -u -b file2.pdf\\n- Embedded fonts and fonts used:\\n  - pdffonts file1.pdf\\n  - pdffonts file2.pdf\\n- Document structure (objects, streams). Tools like mutool:\\n  - mutool show file1.pdf\\n  - mutool show file2.pdf\\n\\n3) Compare visuals (render differences)\\n- Visual diff tools:\\n  - diff-pdf file1.pdf file2.pdf (produces an image diff)\\n  - If not available, render pages to PNGs (e.g., using Ghostscript) and diff images with an image diff tool.\\n- Quick page-by-page comparison: render corresponding pages side-by-side and look for differences in layout, spacing, or embedded media.\\n\\n4) Compare fonts and glyphs specifically\\n- Check for font differences or substitutions:\\n  - pdffonts file1.pdf\\n  - pdffonts file2.pdf\\n- If same fonts but different embedding, you may see differences in rendering or subset status.\\n\\n5) Automated Python-based comparison (optional)\\n- Extract per-page text and compare with a script that reports:\\n  - exact match vs. near-match\\n  - differences in per-page word counts\\n  - line-break and whitespace normalization\\n- Libraries: PyPDF2 or pdfminer.six for text; python-diff-match-patch for diffs.\\n\\n6) What to do if you have two PDFs\\n- If you share the two actual PDFs (or allow me to walk you through commands with your files), I can:\\n  - Run a per-page text diff and report exact page(s) with differences.\\n  - Compare metadata, fonts, and XMP metadata.\\n  - Generate a visual diff to highlight rendering differences.\\n  - Provide a concise summary of any detected differences (content, metadata, or rendering).\\n\\nWhy this matters\\n- Two PDFs can have identical visible text but differ in:\\n  - hidden metadata, creation dates, or authorship\\n  - embedded fonts or font subsets\\n  - non-visible characters (zero-width spaces, different whitespace)\\n  - images, annotations, or links\\n- A thorough diff ensures you catch all of these.\\n\\nIf you want, tell me:\\n- Do you want me to guide you through running these steps on your machine, or would you like me to analyze two PDFs you provide?\\n- Do you prefer a quick textual diff, or a full metadata/structure/visual diff?\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"role\": \"assistant\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"parallel_tool_calls\": true,\n  \"presence_penalty\": 0.0,\n  \"previous_response_id\": null,\n  \"prompt_cache_key\": null,\n  \"prompt_cache_retention\": \"in_memory\",\n  \"reasoning\": {\n    \"context\": \"current_turn\",\n    \"effort\": \"medium\",\n    \"mode\": \"standard\",\n    \"summary\": null\n  },\n  \"safety_identifier\": null,\n  \"service_tier\": \"default\",\n  \"store\": false,\n  \"temperature\": 1.0,\n  \"text\": {\n    \"format\": {\n      \"type\": \"text\"\n    },\n    \"verbosity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\",\n  \"tool_usage\": {\n    \